fit insurers, is failing too many people on affordability and accessibility. We've seen cooperatives work at scale in other countries. We've seen small ones work in the U.S. when given half a chance. So the question might be: what's the better alternative? If not cooperatives, then what? I'd rather try something that has a real track record of success elsewhere and a plausible path forward here than accept a system that leaves too many people struggling to afford the care they need.
