t sure. But I am sure that doing nothing—or only doing half-measures—will leave us with the same broken system. The real choice isn't between perfect cooperatives and the status quo. It's between making a serious, structural effort to create real competition and affordability, or accepting that giant insurers will continue to dominate and premiums will keep rising. If you're not convinced cooperatives are the answer, I respect that. What would you say is a better path to improving accessibility and affordability?
